  {
    "id": 1226075049,
    "node_id": "PRR_kwDOAFgnJc5JFGup",
    "user": {
      "login": "MattiasBuelens",
      "id": 649348,
      "node_id": "MDQ6VXNlcjY0OTM0OA==",
      "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/649348?u=f9d3a0e27ad6727798ececf8936ed59540489c25&v=4",
      "gravatar_id": "",
      "url": "https://api.github.com/users/MattiasBuelens",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/MattiasBuelens",
      "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/MattiasBuelens/followers",
      "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/MattiasBuelens/following{/other_user}",
      "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/MattiasBuelens/gists{/gist_id}",
      "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/MattiasBuelens/starred{/owner}{/repo}",
      "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/MattiasBuelens/subscriptions",
      "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/MattiasBuelens/orgs",
      "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/MattiasBuelens/repos",
      "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/MattiasBuelens/events{/privacy}",
      "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/MattiasBuelens/received_events",
      "type": "User",
      "user_view_type": "public",
      "site_admin": false
    },
    "body": "LGTM.\r\n\r\n> Two thoughts:\r\n> \r\n> 1. I don't understand how \"read all bytes\" works as it doesn't seem to yield to the event loop.\r\n\r\nIf the stream has unread chunks, the read loop of \"read all bytes\" will immediately process all of those without yielding. Afterwards, the read request from the read loop will sit in the reader's queue until *something else* calls [\"enqueue\"](https://streams.spec.whatwg.org/#readablestream-enqueue). This will synchronously call the \"chunk steps\" of that read request (through [step 3 in ReadableStreamDefaultControllerEnqueue](https://streams.spec.whatwg.org/commit-snapshots/f894acdd417926a2121710803cef593e15127964/#readable-stream-default-controller-enqueue)) and advance the read loop.\r\n\r\nSo indeed, we don't yield to any particular event loop, instead we assume that there's some other event loop out there that's calling \"enqueue\", and we run the \"chunk steps\" as part of that same call.",
